REGULATORY BASIS
Use the version of Regulation (EC) No 1272/2008, Annex VIII, applicable at the time of assessment and current ECHA guidance. Under Part A 4.1–4.2, a standard group submission requires identical finished-mixture HEALTH AND PHYSICAL hazard classifications, the SAME COMPONENTS as identified under Part B 3.2, and the SAME reported concentration range for each component. Different environmental hazards or EuPCS categories alone do not automatically prevent grouping. Part A 4.3 has a separate derogation for differences confined to perfumes with TOTAL DIFFERING PERFUMES <=5% per mixture; do not automatically use this in default Mode 1. Do not confuse perfume grouping with generic perfume/colouring identifiers, interchangeable component groups (ICGs), or special formulas. These other rules require their own evidence and legal checks.

